  "publicacion": {
    "titulo": "The Nvidia co-founder who sold every share",
    "descripcion": "Curtis Priem co-founded Nvidia in 1993 and was its chief technical officer until 2003. He retired and had sold all of his shares by 2006. Forbes estimated in 2023 that, had he held, he'd be worth about $70 billion; his actual fortune was about $30 million. He gave $40 million to Rensselaer, his old college. Today Jensen Huang stepped down and Nvidia slid. But hindsight cheats: in the late 90s, 3dfx looked unbeatable, and it went bust.\n\nSources: Rensselaer ECSE Hall of Fame; Forbes (Nov 2023); Wikipedia (Curtis Priem, 3dfx); NBC News (Nov 12, 2026). Not financial advice.",
    "tags": [
      "curtis priem",
      "nvidia",
